   "summary": "The opportunity solution tree is a visual framework used to structure the opportunity space and solutions. It helps product teams shift from an output focus to an outcome focus. The framework is challenging to apply in practice because it requires teams to differentiate between the problem space and the solution space.",
   "summary_citation_ids": ["S1", "S6"],
   "sections": [
      {
         "heading": "What is an opportunity solution tree?",
         "content": "An opportunity solution tree is a visual framework used to structure the opportunity space and solutions. It's a tree visual that starts with an outcome at the root, branches into the opportunity space, and then branches into solutions.",
         "citation_ids": ["S1"]
      },
      {
         "heading": "The purpose of the opportunity solution tree",
         "content": "The purpose of the opportunity solution tree is to add structure to the complex problem of figuring out what to build by starting from an outcome.",
         "citation_ids": ["S1"]
      },
      {
         "heading": "The challenge of structuring the opportunity space",
         "content": "The challenge of structuring the opportunity space is that many teams struggle to differentiate between the problem space and the solution space. Most people write opportunities as solutions, and it's hard to teach people to be comfortable with staying in the problem space.",
         "citation_ids": ["S6"]
      },
      {
         "heading": "How to apply the opportunity solution tree",
         "content": "To apply the opportunity solution tree, teams need to interview customers, collect stories, and structure the opportunity space using an experience map. They need to differentiate between the problem space and the solution space, and make sure to write opportunities in a way that describes the problem.",
         "citation_ids": ["S4", "S5", "S6"]
      },
      {
         "heading": "Challenges of implementing the opportunity solution tree",
         "content": "Implementing the opportunity solution tree can be challenging because it requires teams to fundamentally shift their job from being told to build features to figuring out what to build based on customer needs. It also requires teams to develop new skills, such as interviewing customers and framing opportunities.",
         "citation_ids": ["S9"]
      },
      {
         "heading": "Using the opportunity solution tree in a growing company",
         "content": "As a company grows, the opportunity solution tree remains the same, but the challenges of implementing it may change. In a larger company, teams need to consider adjacent teams and dependencies, and make sure to share their discovery work and be aware of what other teams are working on.",
         "citation_ids": ["S11"]
      }
   ],
