      {
         "heading": "Causes of Misleading A/B Test Results",
         "content": "Sample ratio mismatches and bots are common causes of A/B test results being misleading. Ronny Kohavi explains that the most common occurrence of a sample ratio mismatch is bots hitting the controller in different proportions. He also mentions data pipelines as another reason for sample ratio mismatches.",
         "citation_ids": ["S1", "S3"]
      },
      {
         "heading": "Importance of Trust in Results",
         "content": "Ronny Kohavi emphasizes the importance of trusting results. He explains that people tend to present results that have a sample ratio mismatch, and it is essential to investigate before drawing conclusions.",
         "citation_ids": ["S1"]
      },
      {
         "heading": "Twyman's Law",
         "content": "Ronny Kohavi mentions Twyman's law, which states that 'if any figure that looks interesting or different is usually wrong.' He advises to investigate before celebrating surprising results.",
         "citation_ids": ["S8"]
      }
   ],
